The idea we all learned in school.

454
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,200
Yes.

455
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:22,480
Class one posits that a fraction of a second after the Big Bang, the universe underwent a period of exponential metric expansion.

456
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:22,920
Okay.

457
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:26,020
Space itself stretched faster than the speed of light.

458
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:37,920
To make this work mathematically, theorists had to introduce an auxiliary scalar field, a completely new hypothetical form of matter called the inflitant, driven by a highly specific potential energy curve.

459
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:41,000
It's like pulling a wrinkled bedsheet from all four corners simultaneously.

460
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:44,620
You stretch the fabric of the sheet rapidly, and the wrinkles disappear.

461
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,560
The surface becomes smooth.

462
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:52,200
But the framework points out a massive flaw here, the underdetermination problem.

463
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:56,200
The issue is that the infligent field is entirely ad hoc.

464
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:57,460
We have never observed it.

465
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,820
And worse, there isn't just one mathematical model that fits the data.

466
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:08,760
There are literally hundreds of viable mathematical potentials that can produce the inflation we see.

467
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:09,340
Oh, wow.

468
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:18,420
When a theory is so flexible that almost any arbitrary mathematical curve can be tweaked to fit the observation, it loses its explanatory power.

469
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:20,360
It's a patch, not a foundation.

470
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:30,500
So because class one felt clumsy, theorists tried to clean it up with class two, geometric smoothing, specifically something called quadratic quantum gravity or QQG.

471
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:30,780
Right.

472
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:31,480
What is this?

473
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:35,320
In class two, theorists wanted to get rid of the magical inflatant matter field.

474
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:44,360
They still fundamentally believed the universe had to expand to get smooth, but they argued this expansion should emerge naturally from the geometry of quantum corrected gravity itself.

475
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:44,720
Okay.

476
00:22:44,940 --> 00:22:49,140
Specifically through a complex mathematical process called renormalization group flow.

477
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,200
Okay, but hold on.

478
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:53,300
If they get rid of the inflaton, how does the math actually work?

479
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:56,820
Because the framework highlights a detail here that is almost comical.

480
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,520
Yeah, the spectator fields.

481
00:22:58,520 --> 00:22:58,880
Right.

482
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:04,080
To make QQG function, the equations require the introduction of spectator matter fields.

483
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:05,140
A lot of them.

484
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:09,480
This is where the ontological burden of standard cosmology becomes staggering.

485
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:23,840
To make the beta functions in QQG produce a viable slow roll trajectory for the universe to expand smoothly, theorists have to arbitrarily inject between 100,000 and 1,000,000 of these spectator fields into the math.

486
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:27,280
Wait, a million invisible fields?

487
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:27,660
Yes.

488
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:28,300
What do they do?

489
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:28,800
Nothing.

490
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:29,500
Nothing.

491
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:30,940
They're dynamically inert.

492
00:23:31,340 --> 00:23:32,760
They sit in the vacuum state.

493
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:38,780
They exist purely as mathematical ballast to balance the equations so the universe can expand the way we want it to.

494
00:23:39,060 --> 00:23:40,000
That is absurd.

495
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:40,320
Yeah.

496
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:47,200
You get rid of one magical inflaton field and replace it with a million invisible fields that don't do anything just to make the math work.

497
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:51,180
It highlights the extreme lengths to which we will go to preserve our core assumptions.

498
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:57,080
In this case, the assumption that metric expansion is the only way to smooth out a universe.

499
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:57,640
Wow.

500
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:03,100
However, to its credit, QQG does provide a strict falsifiable prediction.

